<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  DealFlow Cadence - the 4-touch homeowner email sequence (cadence.py), daily at 10:00.

  THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE, NOT AN EXPORT, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT.
  desktop-setup/tasks/ is gitignored (see .gitignore line 301): a Windows-exported task XML carries
  the exporting machine's principal SID and its user paths, so those travel in the transfer bundle
  and never in git. That is correct, and it is also exactly why "DealFlow Cadence" was never in the
  installer's set: there was nowhere in the repo to put a task. This directory is that place.
  install-tasks.ps1 reads templates from here, substitutes the three placeholders below against the
  machine it is running on, and registers them alongside anything found in tasks/. An export in
  tasks/ with the same task name always wins - it carries hardening won on a live box.

  Placeholders, substituted by install-tasks.ps1:
      __REPO__     the resolved checkout on this machine
      __PROFILE__  this machine's %USERPROFILE%
      __USER__     DOMAIN\user, also passed to Register-ScheduledTask -User

  SETTINGS THAT ARE DELIBERATE:

  * StartWhenAvailable is TRUE, with WakeToRun. MACHINE-HANDOFF.md section 4 records that the four
    tasks with StartWhenAvailable=false are silently skipped forever if the machine is asleep at the
    trigger. A skipped cadence run is not neutral: a due step just does not go out, and the owner's
    sequence stalls mid-sequence. So it catches up - and cadence-daily.bat refuses to send outside
    08:00-20:00, which is what makes catching up safe. Do not set this false without deleting that
    guard, and do not delete that guard while this is true.
  * DisallowStartIfOnBatteries / StopIfGoingOnBatteries are FALSE. Six of the eight pipeline tasks
    have them true, which on the armed LAPTOP means skipped on battery and killed mid-run if you
    unplug. Killed mid-run here means some owners mailed, some not, and the state file half written.
  * MultipleInstancesPolicy IgnoreNew. Two cadence runs at once would both read cadence_state.json,
    both decide the same steps are due, and mail them twice.
  * The Command is cadence-daily.bat, NEVER cadence-run.bat. cadence-run.bat ends in `pause`.
  * ExecutionTimeLimit PT2H. The run polls IMAP once per enrolled owner, so it is not instant; PT2H
    is slack, not an expectation. PT6H is for the rebuild/publish jobs and is wrong here - an
    outreach job that has been running six hours is a job to kill.
  * 10:00 IS A DEPENDENCY, NOT A PREFERENCE. This task must run AFTER DealFlow Replies, because
    replies.py then optout_sync.py is what carries a detected STOP into optouts.json, and cadence
    re-reads that ledger on every run - a queue exported yesterday knows nothing about a homeowner
    who said stop this morning. It was 09:00 while Replies fired at 06:45. Replies moved to 08:45
    on 2026-09-22 (confirmed on the laptop), which left a fifteen-minute gap on a job that also
    rebuilds and publishes the board, so this moved to 10:00 with it. If Replies ever moves again,
    MOVE THIS TOO: cadence has no ledger-staleness gate of its own (send_server./send refuses an
    optouts.json older than 2 days; cadence does not), so the ordering is the only thing enforcing
    it. _taskinstalltest.py asserts the gap against a REPLIES_AT constant IN THE TEST - the live
    Replies trigger is in gitignored desktop-setup/tasks/, so the suite catches an edit to this
    file and cannot catch Replies moving. Move both together.
-->
<Task version="1.2" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Author>__USER__</Author>
    <URI>\DealFlow Cadence</URI>
    <Description>DealFlow: send the day's due 4-touch follow-up steps (cadence.py) and poll for replies. Sends real email to homeowners. Only the armed machine may run this - see MACHINE-HANDOFF.md section 1.</Description>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Triggers>
    <CalendarTrigger>
      <StartBoundary>2026-09-19T10:00:00</StartBoundary>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ScheduleByDay>
        <DaysInterval>1</DaysInterval>
      </ScheduleByDay>
    </CalendarTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <UserId>__USER__</UserId>
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
      <RunLevel>LeastPrivilege</RunLevel>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <AllowHardTerminate>true</AllowHardTerminate>
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
    <RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>true</RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>
    <IdleSettings>
      <StopOnIdleEnd>false</StopOnIdleEnd>
      <RestartOnIdle>false</RestartOnIdle>
    </IdleSettings>
    <AllowStartOnDemand>true</AllowStartOnDemand>
    <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    <Hidden>false</Hidden>
    <RunOnlyIfIdle>false</RunOnlyIfIdle>
    <WakeToRun>true</WakeToRun>
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT2H</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <Priority>7</Priority>
  </Settings>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>__REPO__\cadence-daily.bat</Command>
      <WorkingDirectory>__REPO__</WorkingDirectory>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>
